WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
Speaker 1: All right, let us waste no time&nbsp;
because we have such an agenda here at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:09.480
start of today's show. Updated numbers for&nbsp;
Democrats and Republicans in the House and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.400
Senate in what now are midterm elections that&nbsp;
are just about six weeks away. Numbers continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:21.180
to improve for Democrats in both the House and&nbsp;
Senate, although Democrats are still not favored&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:28.560
to win in the House. Let's look at the numbers in&nbsp;
the FiveThirtyEight forecast for the Senate 2022.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:37.560
It is now a 71% chance that Democrats will win and&nbsp;
only a 29% chance that Republicans will win. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:44.460
most likely outcomes are Democrats maintaining a&nbsp;
5050 majority because Kamala Harris would be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:50.940
tie breaking vote vote or Democrats having a 51&nbsp;
to 49 advantage. The way that these numbers have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:56.460
changed over the last several months is directly&nbsp;
in the favor of Democrats. As you can see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:01.440
if you're looking at the screen, at the beginning&nbsp;
of June, Democrats had about a 40% chance of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:09.180
holding the Senate. That has climbed steadily&nbsp;
to a new high of 71%. Now, things that happened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:16.860
29% of the sorry, things that are 29% likely to&nbsp;
happen. Happened 29 out of every 100 times. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:21.600
that doesn't mean that there is any guarantee&nbsp;
here. But right now, the most mathematically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:28.980
likely scenario is Democrats holding the Senate&nbsp;
either 5050 or 51 to 49. Now, over in the House,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:36.420
the numbers are not looking as good for Democrats,&nbsp;
but the numbers are closing in on basically a 2 to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:43.080
1 likelihood of Republicans taking the House,&nbsp;
which is far worse for Republicans than it has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:50.100
been at any previous point during this election&nbsp;
cycle. 28% chance for Democrats. And again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:55.860
if we look at how those numbers have shifted over&nbsp;
time, you will see that what was at one point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:02.340
a 14% chance for Democrats, at one point a 12%&nbsp;
chance for Democrats has now surged all the way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:11.880
up to a 28% chance. Again, the most likely outcome&nbsp;
is still that the Republicans will take control of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:19.740
the House, but the likelihood of that has declined&nbsp;
steadily for a period of June, July, August,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:27.240
three and a half months, three and a half months,&nbsp;
as we've said before, if at this same rate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:35.520
the numbers continue to improve for Democrats.&nbsp;
By Election Day, it would be close to 5050.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:40.140
We don't know that that's going to happen,&nbsp;
but that's the way the numbers look today.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:47.280
And the important thing is everyone must vote.&nbsp;
Do not concede any seat. Fight for everything.

